; Freeing a region of no length leaves the address space map and the page hash
; table of the regions around it alone (sys/ucadr/uc-storage-allocation.lisp
; FREE-REGION and UPDATE-REGION-PHT, docs/release-1003.md).  Load
; lisp/zero-length-region.lisp first.  The cold load gives FASL-TEMP-AREA, the
; last area, a region of no length at the end of its areas, where the next region
; made begins (in the bands of Systems 1001 to 1003, one of WORKING-STORAGE-AREA's);
; a full GC frees it once FASL-TEMP-AREA has another region.  Before the fix,
; FREE-REGION took that quantum out of the address space map, and the machine
; halted at GET-MAP-BITS+13 ("Region not found") in the third case.
;
; The band has such a region, and its origin is in another region.
(eq (si:area-name (zlr-area (zlr-region))) 'si:fasl-temp-area) => T
(let ((r (zlr-region))) (not (member (%region-number (si:region-origin r)) (list nil r)))) => T
; Free it: the other region keeps its quantum, and the page below stays in core.
(zlr-free (zlr-region)) => (T T T)
; The other region's area is still found, as ROOM and the GC look it up.
(progn (with-output-to-string (standard-output) (room)) t) => T
